WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT COVER

The MIT licence above covers the code: the components, scripts, styles, build
tooling and the Worker. Take it, learn from it, build your own OS-desktop site
with it.

It does not cover the content, which is not mine to give away and is not the
useful part anyway:

  - The case studies in src/content/projects, and any client names in them
  - The photographs, avatar and wallpaper
  - The desktop icons in public/icons, which were drawn by hand
  - The voice recording in public/audio
  - "Yves Kwameh" as a name, and the likeness in the avatar

Third-party assets keep their own licences, which travel with them:

  - Space Mono is under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. See public/fonts/OFL.txt.
  - Pixelarticons is MIT. See https://pixelarticons.com
  - The tool logos in src/icons/stack are trademarks of their respective owners,
    reproduced to identify the tools used, not to imply any endorsement.
